WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
Do you know we've talked a lot on this show

2
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.930
about vintage shopping for clothes?

3
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.310
It's made a huge comeback.

4
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.440
But it's not just for clothes,

5
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.667
people are doing it with other things too.

6
00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.250
"Vogue" reports the secondhand market for furniture

7
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.800
is really on fire.

8
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.570
Online resellers, like Chairish,

9
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.550
say business has grown 60%, Drew.

10
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.090 line:15%
People want cheaper, sustainable furnishings,

11
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.700 line:15%
and they don't care if it's brand new.

12
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.500 line:15%
It's a great way to find special items at a discount.

13
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.240 line:15%
I do this all the time in Palm Springs.

14
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.840 line:15%
I'm always on the lookout for like a vintage chair.

15
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.150 line:15%
Well, that's a great destination for vintage shopping.

16
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.610 line:15%
Totally, I even bought a pickup, Drew.

17
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.370 line:15%
Do you know I drive a pickup, mm-hmm,

18
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.400
in Palm Springs, oh, yeah.

19
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.709
Can we put like a just married sign on it

20
00:00:39.709 --> 00:00:42.110
with a bunch of the cans hanging off the back?

21
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.450
Please.
I'll decorate it.

22
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.260
Okay, with the leftover flowers.

23
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.480
Yeah.

24
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.700
But I do, I love it.

25
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.210
I love finding a one of a kind piece.

26
00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.230
You know?
Yeah.

27
00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.130
I found these end tables

28
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.810
at a thrift store called Angel View.

29
00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.643
It's a charity thrift store.

30
00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:58.040
And I bought them for like $35,

31
00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:58.890
and then I Googled them

32
00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.030
and they were worth like almost $1,000.

33
00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.240
You know, you can find amazing things out in the world

34
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.430
if you just sort of go through the stores.

35
00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.770
Clap of hands, who's into vintage shopping?

36
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.680
Oh, yeah.
(audience clapping)

37
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.597
Clap of hands, who is like,

38
00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:17.808
"I am not putting my butt on that used couch?"

39
00:01:17.808 --> 00:01:20.542
(small group clapping)

40
00:01:20.542 --> 00:01:21.913
I like it, ladies.

41
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.540
And you're like really in cahoots about it, which is great.

42
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.123 line:15%
(upbeat music)

